# Round 73: the round-72 counter bound guarded BASES when the axis that
# matters is the REACHABLE VALUE -- a counter stepped by 1e9 for 100
# iterations reaches 1e11 with every assignment passing the base guard,
# and `i * i` wrapped the signed long (VM 1e+22; AOT 1.86e+18, both rc 0,
# plus UB). is_counter now bounds |base| + |step| * 1e8 (the VM's own
# cumulative loop cap, EigenScript#772) under 3e9, so pairwise products
# stay under 2^63; this counter demotes to the double path and prints the
# VM's numbers. Step-1 counters from small bases (the matmul shape) stay
# int -- t22 pins that half.
i is 0
for k in range of 100:
    i is i + 1000000000
print of (i * i)
j is 0
j is j + 2000000000
j is j + 2000000000
j is j + 2000000000
print of (j * j)
